    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="10">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 10</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="314" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.21-2"/> burhbota<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.22-2"/> ⁊ bricbota ⁊ scipforðunga aginne man georne, ⁊ fyrdunga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.23-2"/> eac swa, á þænne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.19-2"/> þearf si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.24-2"/> for gemænelicre neode.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="314" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ burhbota ⁊ brycgbota heonan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="†" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.dagger"/> forð ⁊ scipforðunga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.4"/> aginne man georne, ⁊ fyrdunga eac swá, á ðonne ðearf sy for mæncliere neode.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="314" ed="#liebermann"/>And burgbota ⁊ bricgbote ⁊ scipforðunga aginne man georne, ⁊ fyrdunga eac swa, á þonne þearf sy for gemenelicre neode.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="315" ed="#liebermann"/>Burhbotam et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.19"/> brigbotam (<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.20"/>ciuitatum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.21"/> et pontium emendatio) et scipforðunga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.22"/> et fyrdunga<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.23"/> (quę nauigii uel expeditionis sonant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#IICn_10.lnote.oe.24"/> apparatum) sedulo procuremus, cum necesse fuerit ad commune regni nostri commodum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="10" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="315" ed="#liebermann"/>Urbium refectiones, nauium profectus incipiamus et proficiamus, cum necesse sit pro communi utilitate.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="10" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="178" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ burhbota ⁊ brycgbota<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_10.robnote.fn.7"/> ⁊ scipforðunga<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#IICn_10.robnote.fn.8"/> aginne man georne ⁊ fyrdunga eac swá, á ðonne ðearf sy for mænelicre<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_10.robnote.fn.9"/> neode.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="258" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And burhbota and bricbota and scipforðunga aginne man georne, and fyrdunga eac swa a þænne þearf si, for gemænelicre neode.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="315" ed="#liebermann"/>Und Festungsherstellungen und Brückenherrichtungen und Schiffsrüstungen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_10.lnote.de.1"/> unternehme man eifrig und ferner Landwehrstellungen, immer wenn es nöthig ist wegen gemeinsamen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_10.lnote.de.2"/> Bedarfs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let the repair of fortresses and the repair of bridges and the equipping of ships be eagerly undertaken, and military service likewise, whenever there is need for the common good.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_10.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="179" ed="#robertson"/>And henceforth the repair of fortifications and bridges, and the preparation of ships and the equipment of military forces likewise shall be diligently undertaken for the common need, whenever the occasion arises.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="259" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And improvements to fortifications and bridges are to be undertaken with care, and also the provisioning of the navy and army as the need arises, for the common good.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="315"><ref target="clause:VIAtr_32-3">VI Atr 32.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 32, 3</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_32-3">VI Atr 32.3</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 10: Cn 1018 22-23  VI Atr 32:3</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-059">Cn 1018 22–23</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 10: Cn 1018 22-23  VI Atr 32:3</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><label>used in I–II Cnut</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-059">Cn 1018 22–23</ref> <quote>Kennedy’s table: VI Æthelred 32.3 | D 22–23 | II Cnut 10</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">B's ‘heonan forð’ belongs to 9 (Liebermann). Liebermann compares VI Atr 32.3.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 315, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">bricbota: B adds heonan forð</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">10; 11; 11, 1 <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">10; 11; 11, 1 lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">manuum <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">manuum Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ceamus <hi rend="italic">Hr. Verf. glaubt</hi> fyrðrige <hi rend="italic">zu lesen?</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ceamus Hr. Did the author think he was reading fyrðrige?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.dagger" n="†" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">s. vor. Anm.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">see previous note</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">spät geänd. in</hi> -fyrð.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered late to -fyrð.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uel <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uel K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">id est <hi rend="italic">fügt T zu</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">id est added by T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">c. et p. e. <hi rend="italic">am Rande Dm; im Text T; fehlt übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">c. et p. e. in the margin Dm; in the text T; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rdu. <hi rend="italic">R;</hi> -rðeru. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rdu. R; -rðeru. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fir. <hi rend="italic">R;</hi> fyrðu. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> firðu. <hi rend="italic">Hk; darüber schreibt</hi> fyrdwite <hi rend="italic">nur Dm, was vielleicht zu c.</hi> 12 <hi rend="italic">gehört</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fir. R; fyrðu. T; firðu. Hk; above it only Dm writes fyrdwite, which perhaps belongs to c. 12</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">315</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sonat <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sonat K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.21-2" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.22-2" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Burgbote ⁊ bricgbote heonon forþ [<hi rend="italic">vgl. B</hi>] ⁊ s. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Burgbote ⁊ bricgbote heonon forþ [cf. B] ⁊ s. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.23-2" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fyrþu. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fyrþu. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.19-2" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðonne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðonne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.oe.24-2" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">314</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy for gemen. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy for gemen. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">forðung</hi> und <hi rend="italic">fyrdung</hi> sind nicht verwandt (gegen Toller 834b). Bestimmtere Frist und Strafe des Enhamer Gesetzes fehlen hier, gewiss absichtlich: vielleicht schien unter dem Dänenkönig die Seewehr weniger dringend.—Über die Trinoda necessitas <hi rend="italic">s. u</hi>. 65</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">forðung</hi> and <hi rend="italic">fyrdung</hi> are not related (against Toller 834b). The more precise time-limit and penalty of the Enham law are lacking here, certainly on purpose: perhaps under the Danish king naval defence seemed less urgent.—On the Trinoda necessitas <hi rend="italic">see below</hi> 65</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_10.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">mæne</hi> B's schon Agsä.: <hi rend="italic">s</hi>. Toller <hi rend="italic">mænsumian</hi>, <hi rend="italic">gemænnes</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B's <hi rend="italic">mæne</hi> is already Anglo-Saxon: <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Toller <hi rend="italic">mænsumian</hi>, <hi rend="italic">gemænnes</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_10.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">353</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VI Atr. 32, 3; II Cn. 65.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_10.robnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">178</biblScope></bibl><label>brycgbota</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">br. heonan forð</hi> B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_10.robnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">178</biblScope></bibl><label>scipforðunga</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Later altered to <hi rend="italic">-fyrð</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_10.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">178</biblScope></bibl><label>mænelicre</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gemæn.</hi> G, Ld; <hi rend="italic">gemen.</hi> A.</seg></note>
      </div>
